                     The _l_a_b_e_l corresponds to an entry in a credentials table,
                     as documented in table(5).  It is used with the
                     “smtp+tls” and “smtps” protocols for authentication.
                     Server certificates for those protocols are verified by
                     default.

             ppkkii _p_k_i_n_a_m_e
                     For secure connections, use the certificate associated
                     with _p_k_i_n_a_m_e (declared in a ppkkii directive) to prove the
                     client's identity to the remote mail server.

